 ### [Stackless Traversal](5202-stackless-traversal.md)
-A ray-traversal algorithm for hierarchical volume structures (such as octrees or N3-trees) that eliminates the need for an explicit stack data structure by recalculating Digital Differential Analyzer (DDA) parameters at every descent and ascent step. It distinguishes itself from sibling methods like [DDA Tree Traversal with Mini-Stack](5244-dda-tree-traversal-with-mini-stack.md) by trading increased computational cost for reduced memory usage and avoidance of stack-related overheads, relying instead on parent pointers stored within the hierarchical structure to navigate back up the tree.
